# Port Plan — Step 03: The Prompt Builder (Ruby → Python)

Port `Boukensha::PromptBuilder`, the five backends (`Anthropic`, `OpenAI`,
`Gemini`, `Ollama`, `OllamaCloud`) and their shared `Backends::Base`, plus the
`UnsupportedModelError`, from the Ruby baseline into the Python step folder —
and rewrite the example so `python/03_prompt_builder/` prints the same
Anthropic payload as `ruby/03_prompt_builder`.

This is the fourth of thirteen steps (`00_config` → `12_context`). Step 03 is
substantively step 02 **plus a serialization layer**: nothing calls an API yet,
we only build the exact hash each provider expects. The registry, context,
tool, and message structures do not change behaviour.

